<title>UK: Canada's CAE bags UK RAF training contract.</title>
<headline>Canada's CAE bags UK RAF training contract.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The British government announced on Tuesday that it had chosen a consortium led by Canada's CAE Electronics to provide ground-based aircrew training for the Royal Air Force's fleet of medium support helicopters.</p>
<p>The consortium also includes two British companies, the Vega Group and the Serco Group.  </p>
<p>The proposed contract would be worth around 275 million pounds over 20 years, over 75 percent of which would be spent in the UK, James Arbuthnot, minister of state for defence procurement, told Parliament.</p>
<p>He said the training would be provided for the defence department's Chinook HC Mk 2 and 3, Merlin HC Mk 3 and Puma HC Mk 1 helicopter crews.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
